## What this is

A standalone stdio plugin that exposes {{name}} records as Animus
[subjects](https://github.com/launchapp-dev/animus-cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/subject-backend-plugins.md).
Workflows dispatch agents over your {{name}} backlog without your team
moving off {{name}}.

## Install

```bash
animus plugin install {{org}}/{{full_name}}
```

This downloads the latest release binary, verifies the SHA256, and
registers `{{full_name}}` with the daemon. Re-run after a release to
upgrade.

## Configure

Set the upstream credentials:

```bash
export {{NAME_UPPER}}_API_TOKEN="<your-api-token>"
# Optional: override the API base URL (useful for self-hosted instances).
export {{NAME_UPPER}}_API_URL="https://api.{{name}}.example/v1"
```

Then wire the plugin into a workflow:

```yaml
# .animus/workflows/standard.yaml
subjects:
  {{name}}-default:
    plugin: {{full_name}}
    config:
      api_token_env: {{NAME_UPPER}}_API_TOKEN
    status_map:
      ready:       ["Backlog", "Todo"]
      in_progress: ["In Progress", "In Review"]
      done:        ["Done"]
      cancelled:   ["Cancelled", "Won't Fix"]

workflows:
  - id: {{name}}-impl
    subject_type: {{name}}-default
    phases: [implementation, review]
```

## Run

```bash
animus daemon start
animus task next --subject-type {{name}}-default
animus workflow run --task-id <id>
```

## Roadmap

The scaffold leaves four `todo!()` bodies in `src/backend.rs`. Implement
them in this order:

- [ ] `SubjectBackend::list` — query the {{name}} API and map results to
      `Vec<Subject>`. Honor `filter.status`, `filter.assignee`, and
      `filter.cursor`.
- [ ] `SubjectBackend::get` — fetch a single record by id.
- [ ] `SubjectBackend::update` — apply a `SubjectPatch` (status change,
      assignee reassignment, comment, custom-field update).
- [ ] `SubjectBackend::watch` — optional real-time subscription via
      webhook bridge or SSE. Polling is fine for v0.1.0.
- [ ] Contract tests against mocked upstream responses (mockito for
      HTTP, captured fixtures for complex cases).
- [ ] Release binaries via the bundled GitHub Actions workflow.

